<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:32:36Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Alexander Zverev faces fresh lawsuit from ex-girlfriend</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f11028cd1d123dbe1e535f3e43c6ef231aa149ff0603e97343069518c2aa1a88</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T15:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/alexander-zverev-faces-fresh-lawsuit-from-ex-girlfriend/a-79990005--d63dbeaa4aae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/alexander-zverev-faces-fresh-lawsuit-from-ex-girlfriend/a-79990005?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">World No. 1 tennis player Alexander Zverev is facing a new lawsuit related to a domestic abuse trial. The lawyer for his ex-girlfriend, Brenda Patea, told DW what the allegations are against the German player.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Pistorius visits Auschwitz memorial in Poland trip</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4de4b6d06ee166adcf3858b9bd3d8bd4006af54fb2015a4f15552711da3edd0e</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:32:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-pistorius-visits-auschwitz-memorial-in-poland-trip/live-79987991--a7bef4a1dbc4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-pistorius-visits-auschwitz-memorial-in-poland-trip/live-79987991?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's defense minister's first stop in Poland was the memorial site of the former Nazi extermination camp Auschwitz-Birkenau. Follow DW for more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Wadephul: 'Coalition of the Willing' talks in Berlin send strong signal to Moscow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0130dbfa108e9153e845fdf30e87ef72db62a713a07c6a6fc890e693435f3ed1</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T13:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wadephul-coalition-of-the-willing-talks-in-berlin-send-strong-signal-to-moscow/a-79990664--ce1ce93ebd6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wadephul-coalition-of-the-willing-talks-in-berlin-send-strong-signal-to-moscow/a-79990664?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German Foreign Minister Wadephul has said the Coalition of the Willing meeting in Berlin sends a clear message to Moscow to take peace talks seriously. He also warned Ukraine should be prepared for peace talks to fail.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Borussia Dortmund bows to fan pressure and end Rheinmetall deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5df9cf2e091c688b1d24a45d893962f4f9018f460bf328069fcb1f49c20d570f</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T15:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/borussia-dortmund-bows-to-fan-pressure-and-end-rheinmetall-deal/a-79980121--2c9b64a964f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/borussia-dortmund-bows-to-fan-pressure-and-end-rheinmetall-deal/a-79980121?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Borussia Dortmund has reluctantly ended its association with a major sponsor after long-term fan protests. They are not the first Bundesliga club to u-turn, as commercial interests clash with politics and fan culture.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp and Wirtz offer glimpse of bright German future</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4eb609db7a52fb8d1cb9333b3dc6b71203805198f33ae17ca685cb4f7d56bf1</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T11:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-and-wirtz-offer-glimpse-of-bright-german-future/a-79968184--a5059b3200c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-and-wirtz-offer-glimpse-of-bright-german-future/a-79968184?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's fall from grace in recent years has seen the team drift away from the fans. But Monday's drubbing of the Netherlands and the impact of Jürgen Klopp, Florian Wirtz and emerging youngsters offers hope.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Tesla planning €3BN investment in German factory to produce Cybercabs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd0f23821059ed0086dd03dfa6352701075b8b56e65b9a2b10be536fe46e7c89</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T16:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tesla-planning-_3bn-investment-in-german-factory-to-produce-cybercabs/a-79961416--56a989627169.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tesla-planning-€3bn-investment-in-german-factory-to-produce-cybercabs/a-79961416?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Elon Musk-owned company is looking to further expand its only European production line. Brandenburg's state leader has welcomed the decision.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be802f4fbe22400806003fdff8c383adf8ff7b793e01664687487bfe0ae129a9</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
